                <pb facs="0480" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/231: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Denmark</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Ives</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-19T17:00:00-04:00">May 19, 1930—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Your 25, May 15, 4 p.m. Does Danish note state that Denmark has renounced
                    liens on all revenues mentioned in Leith-Ross’ letter of April 16 or only on
                    customs and tobacco revenues? United States Treasury must have unambiguous
                    statement on which to base its action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
